import AxQM.Concrete.DeutschControlledReachable
import AxQM.Concrete.DeutschSingleQubitUniversality
import AxQM.Concrete.SingleQubitWire

/-!
# Concrete: single-qubit universality of the Deutsch gate on a register wire (N&C Ex 4.44)

Every statement is about matrices — the `2 × 2` rotations/gates (`rotX`, `sMatrix`), Mathlib's
`Submonoid`, and the wire gate `singleQubitOnWire` on an encoded `m`-qubit register.

## The single-qubit half of the §4.5 assembly, for the Deutsch gate

The universality of the Deutsch gate `G = C²(iR_x(πα))` (Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 4.44) is
assembled — following Exercise 4.43 — from a **matrix-level** development
(`Concrete/FourGateUniversality.lean`): every register unitary decomposes into `CNOT`/`Toffoli`
and *uncontrolled single-qubit gates on wires* (`singleQubitOnWire`, the exact decomposition
`exists_isToffoliOrSingleQubit_list_prod_eq`), and each single-qubit factor is approximated up to
a global phase by the reachable single-qubit gates
(`exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure`).

Exercise 4.43's reachable single-qubit gates were the finite products of the two fixed rotations
`R_z(±θ), R_x(±θ)` (`reachableRotations`, `cos θ = 3/5`). The Deutsch gate reaches a **different**
single-qubit set, and its density comes from two *dense* perpendicular axes rather than two fixed
rotations:

* a **dense `x`-axis**: iterating `G` on its doubly-controlled subspace runs the orbit
  `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩ = {iⁿ R_x(nπα)}` (`deutschTargetOrbit`), whose closure holds *every* `R_x(β)` when
  `α` is irrational (`rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`), lifted to the doubly-controlled gate
  `C²(R_x(β))` in `Concrete/DeutschDoublyControlledReachable.lean`;
* the **phase gate `S = diag(1, i)`** (`sMatrix`): reached from the *once*-controlled Deutsch gate
  — the accumulated phase `i` becomes `S` on the control (`sMatrixKron_mem_closure_…`,
  `Concrete/DeutschControlledReachable.lean`), and `S` conjugates the `x`-axis to the perpendicular
  `y`-axis (`sMatrix_mul_rotX_mul_conjTranspose`, `S R_x(β) S† = R_y(β)`).

## The construction and results

* `deutschWireGateSubmonoid α` — the submonoid of single-qubit gates the Deutsch gate reaches on a
  wire, generated by the target orbit `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩` (the dense `x`-axis) together with the phase
  gate `S` and its adjoint `S†` (the second axis). Both generating families are established as
  reachable from `G` — the orbit by `rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx` /
  `ccontrolledMat_rotX_mem_closure_…`, the phase gate `S` by
  `sMatrixKron_mem_closure_deutschControlledReachableMats`.
* `rotX_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid` / `sMatrix_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid` /
  `sMatrix_conjTranspose_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid` — the two dense axes lie in the
  submonoid's closure (the orbit is a generating subset, so `rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`
  transfers by `closure_mono`; `S`, `S†` are generators).
* `exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid` — **single-qubit universality of the
  Deutsch gate set, up to a global phase**: for every `U ∈ U(2)` some global phase `e^{iα₀}` makes
  `e^{iα₀} U` a closure limit of `deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`. The dense `x`-axis and `S` are
  exactly the two hypotheses of the single-qubit core
  `exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_of_forall_rotX_sMatrix`, which recovers the `y`-axis from
  `S R_x S† = R_y` and closes the Euler decomposition.
* `exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid` — **the same, kept
  phase-clean on a chosen wire** of the `m`-qubit register: for every wire `j` and `U ∈ U(2)`,
  some global phase makes `e^{iα₀} • singleQubitOnWire enc j U` a limit of `singleQubitOnWire enc
  j` applied to `deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`. This is the Deutsch counterpart of Exercise 4.43's
  `exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure`: the map `singleQubitOnWire enc j` is
  continuous and the phase pulls out *globally* (`singleQubitOnWire_smul`), so the residual phase
  survives as a genuine global phase on the whole register — the property the §4.5.3 error-chaining
  assembly needs.

This is the single-qubit part of the §4.5 register assembly for the Deutsch gate (compare the
reversible gates `CNOT`/`Toffoli`, `Concrete/DeutschControlledReachable.lean` /
`DeutschDoublyControlledReachable.lean`). It packages *which* single-qubit gates `G` reaches and
their density; these gates arise on register wires from the `x`-axis with the two control wires
held at `|1⟩` (ancillas) and the phase gate `S` from a control-wire placement.
-/

namespace AxQM.Concrete

open Matrix

variable {m d : ℕ}

/-- **The Deutsch single-qubit gate submonoid** (Nielsen & Chuang, Exercise 4.44). The submonoid of
`2 × 2` gates generated by the Deutsch target orbit `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩` (`deutschTargetOrbit`) together
with the phase gate `S = diag(1, i)` (`sMatrix`) and its adjoint `S†` — the two families whose
closure supplies the two dense perpendicular single-qubit axes the Deutsch gate `G = C²(iR_x(πα))`
reaches: a dense `x`-axis from iterating `G` (`rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`) and the phase gate `S`
from `G`'s control structure (`sMatrixKron_mem_closure_deutschControlledReachableMats`). Its closure
fills `U(2)` up to a global phase (`exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid`). -/
noncomputable def deutschWireGateSubmonoid (α : ℝ) : Submonoid (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) :=
  Submonoid.closure (deutschTargetOrbit α ∪ {sMatrix, sMatrix.conjTranspose})

/-- The Deutsch target orbit `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩` is a generating subset of `deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`,
hence contained in it. -/
theorem deutschTargetOrbit_subset_deutschWireGateSubmonoid (α : ℝ) :
    deutschTargetOrbit α ⊆ (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)) :=
  Set.subset_union_left.trans Submonoid.subset_closure

/-- **The dense `x`-axis lies in the submonoid's closure.** When `α` is irrational, every
`x`-rotation `R_x(β)` is a closure limit of `deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`: it is a closure limit of
the target orbit `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩` (`rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx`), which is a generating subset of the
submonoid, so `closure_mono` transfers the density. -/
theorem rotX_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) (β : ℝ) :
    rotX β ∈ closure (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)) :=
  closure_mono (deutschTargetOrbit_subset_deutschWireGateSubmonoid α)
    (rotX_mem_closure_cyclic_iRx hα β)

/-- **The phase gate `S` lies in the submonoid's closure** — it is one of the two extra generators,
hence in the submonoid, hence in its closure. -/
theorem sMatrix_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid (α : ℝ) :
    sMatrix ∈ closure (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)) :=
  subset_closure (Submonoid.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_right _ (by simp)))

/-- **The adjoint phase gate `S†` lies in the submonoid's closure** — it is the other extra
generator, hence in the submonoid, hence in its closure. -/
theorem sMatrix_conjTranspose_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid (α : ℝ) :
    sMatrix.conjTranspose
      ∈ closure (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)) :=
  subset_closure (Submonoid.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_right _ (by simp)))

/-- **Single-qubit universality of the Deutsch gate set, up to a global phase** (Nielsen & Chuang,
Exercise 4.44, single-qubit content). When `α` is irrational, for every single-qubit unitary
`U ∈ U(2)` some global phase `e^{iα₀}` makes `e^{iα₀} U` a closure limit of
`deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`.

The submonoid's closure contains every `x`-rotation and the phase gate `S` (with its adjoint),
which are exactly the hypotheses of the single-qubit core
`exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_of_forall_rotX_sMatrix`: the `y`-rotations are recovered from
`S R_x(β) S† = R_y(β)`, giving two perpendicular dense axes, and the corrected generalized Euler
decomposition then covers all of `U(2)` up to a global phase. -/
theorem exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α)
    {U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ} (hU : U ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) :
    ∃ a : ℝ, Complex.exp ((a : ℂ) * Complex.I) • U
      ∈ closure (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)) :=
  exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_of_forall_rotX_sMatrix (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α)
    (rotX_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid hα)
    (sMatrix_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid α)
    (sMatrix_conjTranspose_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid α) U hU

/-- **Single-qubit universality of the Deutsch gate on a register wire, kept phase-clean** (Nielsen
& Chuang, Exercise 4.44). When `α` is irrational, for every wire `j` of the `m`-qubit register and
every single-qubit unitary `U ∈ U(2)`, some global phase `e^{iα₀}` makes
`e^{iα₀} • singleQubitOnWire enc j U` a closure limit of `singleQubitOnWire enc j` applied to the
Deutsch single-qubit submonoid `deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`.

This is the Deutsch counterpart of Exercise 4.43's
`exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure`: a one-line application of the shared generic
per-wire transport
`exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure_of_exists_phase_smul_mem_closure`
(`Concrete/SingleQubitWire.lean`) to the `2 × 2` universality
`exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid`. The transport keeps the residual phase
global on the uncontrolled wire (`singleQubitOnWire_smul`), the phase-clean property the §4.5
error-chaining assembly needs. -/
theorem exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid {α : ℝ}
    (hα : Irrational α) (enc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (j : Fin m)
    {U : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ} (hU : U ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) :
    ∃ a : ℝ, Complex.exp ((a : ℂ) * Complex.I) • singleQubitOnWire enc j U
      ∈ closure (singleQubitOnWire enc j ''
        (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ))) :=
  exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure_of_exists_phase_smul_mem_closure enc j
    (exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid hα hU)

end AxQM.Concrete
